<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles I of England</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1600">1600</a>–<a href="/years/1649">1649</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Charles I of Scotland</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles I was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> and Ireland from 1625 to 1649. His attempt to impose a new prayer book on Scotland in 1637 provoked the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-covenant">National Covenant</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishops-wars">Bishops' Wars</a>, which forced him to recall the English Parliament and led to the civil wars of the 1640s. Defeated by Parliament's armies, he was tried and executed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> on 30 January 1649.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-i-of-england.jpg" alt="Charles I of England" width="320" height="553" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Workshop of Anthony van Dyck · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Charles_I_after_original_by_van_Dyck.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
